<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins 26 mln Ecu Finnish turbine order.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins 26 mln Ecu Finnish turbine order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC-Alsthom said on Thursday it had won an order worth 26 million Ecus to supply a steam turbine generator and other equipment for extension of Finland's Vaskiluoto cogeneration plant.</p>
<p>The plant, supplying electricity and heat to the city of Vaasa on the Gulf of Bothnia, will be fully operational at the end of 1998, said a statement from the group, a joint venture between Britain's General Electric Co Plc and France's Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
